(Whether the compiler has the fixes voxelf needs. They are on Vox main and
 in no release up to 0.4.16: docs/bugs/unreleased.md, #128, #156 and #160.
 Each part prints what a compiler with its fix prints, and build.sh compares
 the whole output, so a compiler without one of them answers differently, or
 stops on a signal, and is refused before voxelf is built with it.)

(#156: a map read out of a list parameter into a local, then appended, is
 the map, as 'place the sections of kind' appends each section it places.)
To 'copy over' with a list called sections and a list called placed.
    a map called section is element 1 of sections.
    append section to placed.

(#128, naming copies: a map named from another is a copy of its own, as the
 trial cursors in 'a fresh page saves memory for' are.)
a map called cursors is {"file": 1}.
a map called 'trial cursors' is cursors.
Set 'trial cursors''s "file" to 2.
a number called 'file cursor' is cursors's "file".
Print "a named map is a copy: {file cursor}".

a list called sections is [{"name": ".text"}].
a list called placed is [].
'copy over' with sections and placed.
Print "a section read out and appended: {placed}".

(#160: the period after an Otherwise closes the chain, and one more closes
 the loop around it, as in 'read the manifest'.)
a number called 'rounds run' is 0.
a number called 'lines run after the loop' is 0.
For each round from 1 to 2,
    If round is 1 then, increment 'rounds run'.
    Otherwise, increment 'rounds run'..
increment 'lines run after the loop'.
Print "after an Otherwise: {rounds run} rounds, then {lines run after the loop} line after the loop".
